<p>
I've recently started a new blog, which is quite fun! It's on a service called <a href="https://handwritten.blog">handwritten.blog</a>. It encourages you to write
your posts physically, then photograph/scan them and upload them to your own blog. It has a nice workflow too, where you can upload via sending a photo in an email.
There's a few things I really like about this. It encourages working at a slower pace, and being able to be with your thoughts without the distraction of a computer.
It also, by it's medium, doesn't necessitate polish. As you can see if you peek at my post history, I've not been writing as much on this blog lately. There's a few reasons
for that, but one of them is that it feels like something needs to be a certain level of 'done' to make it to this blog. Whereas I am free to sketch/write to my handwritten
blog and it feels fun, and lacks pressure.
</p>
<p>
All of this really is to say two things: 1. Go check out my <a href="https://etopiei.handwritten.blog/">handwritten blog</a>! 2. I'm enjoying it, and I might be posting there a little more with unfinished/scattered thoughts.
</p>
<p>
Endnote: It also has so many nice thoughtful features. RSS feed is built in, you can annotate your pictures with the posts' text (for screen readers and better accessibility), and you can interactively 'draw' on the image to create links within the picture (which I used to back-link to this blog in my first post).
</p>
<p>
- etopiei
(12/10/2026)
</p>